hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16671","He said: Abu Said narrated to us, Umar ibn Farrukh narrated to us, he said: Musab ibn Nuh al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: I met an old woman of ours who was among those who pledged to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: We came to him one day, and he took upon us that we shall not wail. The old woman said: O Messenger of Allah, some people had assisted me in a calamity that befell me, and a calamity befell them, and I wish to assist them. Then she came to him and pledged to him, and said: It is the right conduct that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, spoke of: Nor disobey you in right conduct."
